  "prompts": {
    "opening": "Use case identity-preserve. Restore the existing Dino Klokkijken world 9 playable pirate dinosaur as one high-detail square 1536×1536 transparent game sprite. Image 1 is the exact canon for pose, left-facing nose, proportions, eye shape and positions, silhouette and framing. Keep its painted soft 3D style and saturated blue skin with dark blue spots, pink cheeks, warm white chin/belly/claws, red tricorne and waistcoat with polished gold edging, two crossed gold cutlasses, gold buttons, brown leather belt with gold buckle, red sail and its brown spar, original red/yellow/green-and-blue parrot holding the same perch. Preserve exact placement and shape of accessories. Image 2 is a high-resolution detail reference ONLY, especially for the missing clock face. Place a complete ivory watch dial with subtle blue index ticks and blue hands inside the existing round gold frame, with gold chain and finial. No numerals or text. Keep feet at the same line, hat/sail/parrot/tail fully visible with the same transparent margins. No stage, shadow outside sprite, fog, checkerboard, motion or effects. Fully opaque interiors, detailed clean alpha silhouette. Exact same recognizable character, no redesign. Do not reflect the source.",
    "answerAndCrouch": "Identity-preserving sprite sheet of the EXACT attached left-facing pirate dino, same eyes, face, body, accessories, parrot seated on its wood perch, gold pocket watch with full ivory dial and neutral readable hands/ticks, red/gold tricorne, red sail and vest, blue skin. Same camera, lighting, painted game art style and character size as reference. Fully transparent outside each sprite, opaque figure, no floor shadow, no lettering, no guides, no ghost effects. Exact uniform 2 columns x 2 rows, four equally sized square cells, no separators, centered full-body figure with safe margin in every cell, same planted sole line in grounded poses, no cell spillover. Use the largest square canvas available. Top-left: both blue hands lifted clearly apart ready to clap, keep eyes and standing legs the same. Top-right: blue palms clearly touch at chest center for the clap, keep eyes and standing legs the same; have parrot stay on perch attached to costume. Bottom-left: wrong-answer disappointed face with closed small frown and brows raised inward, arms down, same standing pose. Bottom-right: deeply crouched bent legs, planted feet, parrot and clock remain present, about to spring.",
