    "turnViews": "Identity-preserving sprite sheet of the EXACT attached left-facing pirate dino, same eyes, face, body, accessories, parrot seated on its wood perch, gold pocket watch with full ivory dial and neutral readable hands/ticks, red/gold tricorne, red sail and vest, blue skin. Same camera, lighting, painted game art style and character size as reference. Fully transparent outside each sprite, opaque figure, no floor shadow, no lettering, no guides, no ghost effects. Exact uniform 2 columns x 2 rows, four equally sized square cells, no separators, centered full-body figure with safe margin in every cell, same planted sole line in grounded poses, no cell spillover. Use the largest square canvas available. Progressing around one vertical axis of rotation from the reference's front-left view, holding a playful dancer's stance, body upright and feet planted at same baseline. Top-left: pure left profile. Top-right: back-left three-quarter angle. Bottom-left: back-right three-quarter angle. Bottom-right: right profile to front-right three-quarter. Show the backside of the costume and sail correctly when turned away, with parrot and clock still attached and occluded naturally. Exactly this row-major order.",
    "rearSideAndFall": "Identity-preserve. Exact same illustrated soft 3D pirate dinosaur as image 1 (matching eyes, blue with darker spots, gold-edged red hat with crossed cutlasses, original sail and parrot with clock). Image 2 indicates four existing angles for turn scale and style. Render exactly four full-body silhouettes on a true transparent background in an exact equal square 2×2 grid, row-major, margins in every cell. Top-left: exactly straight REAR view, no snout or eyes at all, centered upright above grounded feet, with rear face of red sail visible. Top-right: exactly pure RIGHT PROFILE with snout pointing right, one eye only, tail left; original hat red and gold and bird and complete clock still carried, feet grounded. Bottom-left: nearly lying on stomach after a harmless fall, front blue palms planted far forward, face low but alert. Bottom-right: halfway back up from the fall, same planted palms and feet, looking forward. Bottom poses face LEFT like image 1. Clock dial ivory with neutral indices and hands, gold ring and chain. Preserve same head size, silhouette identity, volume and lighting above; clean alpha with no silhouette halo, props touching character, no checkerboard, no shadows or effects outside sprites, no lettering or guide lines."
